# .gitignore for a git-backed Obsidian vault.
#
# Copy this to the root of the vault repository. Two things drive every rule
# here: keeping per-machine state out of a repo that two machines push to, and
# keeping plugin caches out of a repo that is meant to stay small enough to
# clone quickly. On the vault this was written for, plugin caches were 91% of
# the directory and a single cache file was 236 MB — committed once, that file
# is in the history forever.

# --- Obsidian per-machine state -------------------------------------------
# Which panes are open, where the cursor is, which file is focused. Changes
# constantly, means nothing to anyone else, and conflicts on every sync.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# Settings themselves (appearance, hotkeys, enabled plugins) ARE tracked, so
# configuration follows the vault to a new machine.

# --- Plugin caches and generated indexes ----------------------------------
# Semantic-search and AI plugins build large local indexes beside the notes.
# They are derived data: regenerable, machine-specific, and enormous.
.smart-env/
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json.bak
.obsidian/plugins/*/*.log

# Embedding/index shards, whatever plugin emits them.
*.ajson

# Copilot-style conversation indexes, which can reach hundreds of megabytes.
.obsidian/copilot-index*.json
.obsidian/**/copilot-index*.json
copilot-index*.json

# --- Nested vaults ---------------------------------------------------------
# A subdirectory with its own .obsidian/ is a separate vault. Track its notes,
# but not its own per-machine state.
**/.obsidian/workspace.json
**/.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json

# --- Obsidian soft-delete --------------------------------------------------
# Deleted notes land here. Git is the undo mechanism now.
.trash/

# --- OS and sync artefacts -------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Icon?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# --- Editor / tooling ------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*~
